# These scripts execute inside the Linux container. On a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true they would arrive as CRLF, and because the Docker build
# context copies the working tree verbatim the shebang becomes "bash\r":
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# Pinning them to LF keeps an image built on Windows identical to one built on
# the recording server.
*.sh text eol=lf
